text:
claire: quick announcement for mobile teams: we're moving Swift SDK streaming and completion APIs to Swift Concurrency (async/await) as the primary surface. we'll deprecate old completion-handler callbacks. heads-up to docs + support. :iphone:

josh: from eng: new API landed in sdk-swift@v4.0.0-rc1. We provide compatibility adapters that wrap the old closures into async functions for a 180-day transition. No runtime changes, just api surface change.

rachel: Docs plan: migration guide, before/after snippets, update quickstarts and playgrounds, and add a deprecation banner on the Swift SDK page. I'll draft the migration examples tonight.

ios-bot: CI: macos builds will run both legacy and async examples for 6 months. We'll enable a compiler warning when legacy callbacks are used.

support: Please create a 3-bullet TL;DR for support and an FAQ for common migration errors (e.g., "ambiguous closure" or missing `@escaping`). Also need a rollback note for Dedicated runtime images.

claire: timeline: today - announce + docs PR wip; 180 days - legacy callback APIs marked deprecated with warning; 365 days - remove legacy APIs in v5.0. Provide extended support for Dedicated/Private on request.

josh: migration example for docs:
```swift
// legacy (completion handler)
client.generate(prompt: "hi") { result in
  switch result {
  case .success(let resp): print(resp.text)
  case .failure(let err): print("error", err)
  }
}

// new (async/await)
Task {
  do {
    let resp = try await client.generate(prompt: "hi")
    print(resp.text)
  } catch {
    print("error", error)
  }
}
```
Note: adapters available: `LegacyAdapter.wrap(client:)` for quick fixes.

pete: Ops note: for Dedicated we'll ship v4 runtime images with the adapter preinstalled and keep legacy images pinned for 12 months. We'll also emit a runtime log when deprecated callbacks are invoked.

rachel: Action owners: rachel -> migration guide + banner; josh -> adapter + CI warnings; support -> TL;DR + FAQ; claire -> customer comms. I'll push the WIP PR and link once merged.

claire: thanks everyone. If you have customers that require more than 12 months, DM me and we'll handle exceptions. :thumbsup:
